Let's find a recursive formula for $f(n)$.

- The first term is the initial size of Daniela's savings, which is $\blue{\$30}$.
- The common difference is the amount Daniela added each week, which is $\pink{\$12}$.

Therefore, this is the recursive definition of the sequence:

$\begin{cases}
f(1)=\blue{30}
\\\\
f(n)=f(n-1)+\pink{12}
\end{cases}$

In conclusion, $f$ is an *arithmetic* sequence.

$\begin{cases}
f(1)=\blue{30}
\\\\
f(n)=f(n-1)+\pink{12}
\end{cases}$
